---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Partners — Base Impact" description="Organizations and businesses partnering with Base Impact to bring technology help to Brevard County, FL.">
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-body mb-4">Partners</h1>
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
    <p>Base Impact works alongside local organizations, churches, pantries, and small nonprofits to bring technology help where it's needed most.</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">How we partner</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Technology setup &amp; support</strong> — Free device setup, security, and ongoing support for 1–5 person community groups.</li>
      <li><strong>Resource sharing</strong> — Our directory lists local services alongside 211, making it easier for neighbors to find help.</li>
      <li><strong>Volunteer coordination</strong> — We connect skilled volunteers with organizations that need tech help.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Cell provider partnerships</h2>
    <p>We are actively seeking partnerships with cellular providers (AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile, and others) to provide free or low-cost phones and tablets to homeless individuals and people in need. Devices come with data plans so recipients can access job portals, housing applications, telehealth, and emergency services.</p>
    <p>If your company provides cellular service and would like to partner with us, please reach out.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Organizations where I volunteer</h2>
    <p>Base Impact's founder has volunteered and provided hands-on service at the following verified tax-exempt organizations in Brevard County. These are not formal partnerships — they are places where I have served and built relationships:</p>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">LifePointe Ministries, Inc.</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">EIN 45-1198607 · Titusville, FL · 501(c)(3)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Operates the Titusville Civic Center. Provides homeless showers, clothing, essentials, toiletries, and Thursday evening dinners. Operates the only inclement-weather cold-night shelter between Titusville and Port Orange. Runs CREW 29 outreach ministry providing meals, clothing, hygiene items, and fellowship. (Fiscal sponsorship pending.)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">No One Hungry, Inc.</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">EIN 83-2834992 · Titusville, FL · 501(c)(3)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Operates the Pine St Food Pantry providing food and basic necessities. Delivers food to homebound seniors. Reaches people experiencing homelessness with food and personal care items.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Hope for North Brevard, Inc.</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">EIN 27-0352718 · Brevard County, FL · 501(c)(3)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Sponsors Under The Bridge Ministries. Provides community support and outreach in North Brevard County.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">The Rock Church</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">EIN 85-2661919 · Mims/Scottsmoor, FL · 501(c)(3)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Congregation serving Brevard County through worship, community events, and outreach to families in need. Planted with the Florida Baptist Convention.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Under The Bridge Ministries</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">Titusville, FL · Sponsored by Hope for North Brevard</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Faith-based outreach serving people experiencing homelessness. Meets Monday evenings under the A. Max Brewer Bridge to share hot meals, blankets, and supplies.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">First United Methodist Church of Titusville</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">Titusville, FL · Church (automatically tax-exempt)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Runs the Community Breakfast program providing food, essentials, clothing, and a safe space to shelter from the weather. Not a full-time shelter — partners with LifePointe Ministries for cold-night shelter overflow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">First Christian Church of Titusville</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-faint">Titusville, FL · Church (automatically tax-exempt)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Congregation serving North Brevard County through worship, fellowship, and practical outreach to families in need.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Technology help provided</h2>
    <p>Base Impact has provided free technology services to partner organizations:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>No One Hungry</strong> — Trained on existing sign-in system for guest registration, applicant intake sheets, and database for tracking food pantry guests</li>
      <li><strong>The Rock Church</strong> — Audio/video system setup, livestreaming, sound board configuration, Wi-Fi, office computers, presentation software, website</li>
      <li><strong>First Christian Church</strong> — Technology needs, computer and internet navigation assistance</li>
      <li><strong>LifePointe Ministries</strong> — Technology support for CREW 29 outreach operations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Community involvement</h2>
    <p>Base Impact's founder is deeply involved in the Brevard County community through hands-on volunteer work at local churches, food pantries, cold-night shelters, and community organizations. This direct experience shapes our programs and ensures we understand the real needs of the people we serve.</p>
    <p>Activities include food service, clothing distribution, shelter security, technology support, senior assistance, housing connections, and emergency response.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">I am building formal partnerships with local organizations. If your organization serves Brevard County and would like to collaborate, please reach out.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Cell provider partnerships</h2>
    <p>We are actively seeking partnerships with cellular providers (AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile, and others) to provide free or low-cost phones and tablets to homeless individuals and people in need. Devices come with data plans so recipients can access job portals, housing applications, telehealth, and emergency services.</p>
    <p>If your company provides cellular service and would like to partner with us, please reach out.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Brevard Homeless Coalition (CoC)</h2>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Brevard Homeless Coalition</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-faint">Brevard County, FL · Continuum of Care (CoC)</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Base Impact Inc. is a new member of the <a href="https://brevardhomelesscoalition.org/coc/" class="text-accent underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brevard Homeless Coalition</a>, the Continuum of Care (CoC) for Brevard County. The CoC coordinates housing and services for people experiencing homelessness, including the annual Point-in-Time count, housing programs, and community-wide planning to end homelessness.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">As a member, Base Impact contributes to community-wide efforts to connect people experiencing homelessness with housing, technology access, and digital skills training.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Upcoming volunteer opportunities</h2>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-10 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Feed Hope Now</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-faint">Brevard County, FL · <a href="https://feedhopenow.org/get-involved/volunteer/" class="text-accent underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">feedhopenow.org</a></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Base Impact's founder is in the process of becoming a volunteer with Feed Hope Now. Account creation in progress. Volunteer activities will include food distribution and community support.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-faint mt-1">Status: Account setup in progress — volunteering not yet started.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Tech company partnerships</h2>
    <p>We are seeking partnerships with technology companies to provide hardware and infrastructure for our programs:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Tablets &amp; laptops</strong> — For hands-on digital skills training and loan programs.</li>
      <li><strong>Desktops &amp; servers</strong> — For local AI generation, document processing, and technology support.</li>
      <li><strong>Parts &amp; components</strong> — For device refurbishment and repair programs.</li>
      <li><strong>Software &amp; licenses</strong> — For nonprofit tech support and training (Microsoft, Google, Adobe, etc.).</li>
      <li><strong>AI hardware</strong> — GPUs, NPUs, and AI-capable workstations for local model inference.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">Potential partners include Microsoft, Google, Apple, Dell, HP, Lenovo, and other technology companies with nonprofit donation programs.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Church &amp; nonprofit partnerships</h2>
    <p>We are seeking partnerships with churches, ministries, and local nonprofits for events, programs, and projects:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Event collaboration</strong> — Joint community events, resource fairs, and technology workshops.</li>
      <li><strong>Program partnerships</strong> — Co-hosting digital skills training, device distribution, and support services.</li>
      <li><strong>Project collaboration</strong> — Working together on community improvement and technology access initiatives.</li>
      <li><strong>Space sharing</strong> — Using church and nonprofit facilities for training sessions and community events.</li>
    </ul>

